.TH "UNCLUTTER\-XFIXES" "1" "07/14/2024" "\ \&" "\ \&"
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * Define some portability stuff
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.\" http://bugs.debian.org/507673
.\" http://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/groff/2009-02/msg00013.html
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el       .ds Aq '
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * set default formatting
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" disable hyphenation
.nh
.\" disable justification (adjust text to left margin only)
.ad l
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * MAIN CONTENT STARTS HERE *
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.SH "نام (NAME)"
unclutter-xfixes \- rewrite of unclutter using the X11\-Xfixes extension
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
unclutter [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR] [\fB\-\-jitter\fR \fIradius\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-scrolling\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-buttons\fR \fIbuttons\fR] [\fB\-\-hide\-on\-touch\fR] [\fB\-\-fork\fR|\fB\-b\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR|\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-hidden\fR]
.sp
Compatibility arguments:
.sp
unclutter [\fB\-\-display\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIdisplay\fR] [\fB\-\-idle\fR \fIseconds\fR] [\fB\-\-keystroke\fR] [\fB\-\-grab\fR] [\fB\-\-noevents\fR] [\fB\-\-reset\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-onescreen\fR] [\fB\-\-not\fR] \fIname \&...\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Hide the mouse cursor if it isn\(cqt being used\&.
.sp
This version of unclutter is a rewrite of the original and uses the x11\-xfixes extension, which means that no fake windows or pointer grabbing is needed\&. This should work better with window managers and applications\&.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.PP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the number of seconds after which the cursor should be hidden if it was neither moved nor any button was pressed\&. (Default: 5)
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-jitter\fR \fIradius\fR
.RS 4
Ignore cursor movements if the cursor hasn\(cqt moved at least
\fIradius\fR
pixels\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-exclude\-root\fR
.RS 4
Don\(cqt hide the mouse cursor if it is idling over the root window and not an actual window since in this case it isn\(cqt obscuring anything important, but rather just the desktop background\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-ignore\-scrolling\fR
.RS 4
Ignore mouse scroll events (buttons 4 and 5) so that scrolling doesn\(cqt unhide the cursor\&. This is a shortcut for
\fB\-\-ignore\-buttons\fR
\fI4,5\fR\&. If you want to ignore horizontal scrolling as well, use
\fB\-\-ignore\-buttons\fR
instead by specifying all buttons manually (e\&.g\&.
\fI4,5,6,7\fR)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-ignore\-buttons\fR
.RS 4
Defines the mouse buttons which do not unhide the cursor when clicked\&. You can pass multiple button numbers by separating them with
\fI,\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-hide\-on\-touch\fR
.RS 4
Hides the mouse cursor on touch events\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-start\-hidden\fR
.RS 4
Starts the cursor hidden\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-fork\fR|\fB\-b\fR
.RS 4
Fork unclutter to the background\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-help|\-h\fR
.RS 4
Display the usage and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR
.RS 4
Display the version and exit\&.
.RE
.SH "TROUBLESHOOTING"
.SS "\-\-ignore\-scrolling doesn\(cqt work"
.sp
This can happen, especially on trackpoints, if other button events, e\&.g\&. for horizontal scrolling, are sent as well\&. You can try adding some jitter, or verify by using \fBxev \-event button\fR\&. If you want to ignore horizontal scrolling as well, use \fB\-\-ignore\-buttons\fR instead of \fB\-\-ignore\-scrolling\fR\&.
.SH "COMPATIBILITY"
.sp
In order to be used as a drop\-in replacement of unclutter, unclutter\-xfixes accepts all command line arguments of unclutter, but ignores most of them\&.
.PP
\fB\-\-display\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIdisplay\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the X display to use\&. The same effect can be achieved by setting the
\fBDISPLAY\fR
environment variable\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-idle\fR \fIseconds\fR
.RS 4
This argument is mapped to
\fB\-\-timeout\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-keystroke\fR
.RS 4
This argument is ignored\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-grab\fR
.RS 4
This argument is ignored\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-noevents\fR
.RS 4
This argument is ignored\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-reset\fR
.RS 4
This argument is ignored\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-root\fR
.RS 4
This argument does the opposite of
\fB\-\-exclude\-root\fR\&. Shouldn\(cqt need to be given, as this is the default behavior in unclutter\-xfixes\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-onescreen\fR
.RS 4
This argument restricts unclutter to the single screen specified in
\fB\-\-display\fR
or to the default screen of the display\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-not\fR
.RS 4
This argument will result in all arguments that aren\(cqt options or option arguments, to be collected into a list that specifies windows where the cursor shall not be removed\&. These will be the windows where an element of the list matches, in a case insensitive comparison, the starting characters of either the WM_NAME, or the name or class of the WM_CLASS, properties of the window\&. (Note that this argument can be given anywhere on the command line\&.)
.RE
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
.PP
\fBIngo Bürk\fR <\&ingo\&.buerk@airblader\&.de\&>
.RS 4
Author.
.RE
